<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<Patch>
    <!-- RULES:
Increase cold, flu, when cooler.
Increase allergies in spring/fall (or equivilent)
Increase maleria when wet and hot
Increase plague when dry(?) and hot

CropBlight - default: .35. Increase when wet.
Alphabeavers - default: .30. Increase on wooded maps.
Flashstorm - default: .3. Increase in when biome would experience forest fires IRL.
ColdSnap - default: 2. Increase in winter/on cold maps.
HeatWave - default: 3. Increase in summer/on hot maps.
VolcanicWinter - default: .08. Increase in lava zone.
HerdMigration - default: .8. Increase in spring/fall in applicable areas.
Special_HerdMigration - default: 0. Use only in areas known for imporant migrations (caribou, savanna).
AmbrosiaSprout - default: .35. Increase in spring?
ManhunterPack - default 2. Increase in winter on cold maps.
AnimalInsanityMass - default 1.3. Increase in winter on cold maps, summer on hot maps.
AnimalInsanitySingle - default 5. Increase in winter on cold maps, summer on hot maps.

					<AnimalInsanityMass>1.3</AnimalInsanityMass>
					<AnimalInsanitySingle>5</AnimalInsanitySingle>
					<HeatWave>3</HeatWave>
					<ColdSnap>2</ColdSnap>
					<CropBlight>.35</CropBlight>
					<Alphabeavers>.3</Alphabeavers>
					<Flashstorm>.3</Flashstorm>
					<AmbrosiaSprout>.35</AmbrosiaSprout>


Most biomes follow this pattern - 
Spring: a little wet. 
Summer: dry
Fall: very wet.
Winter: wet.
-->

